WEBVTT

00:22:58.906 --> 00:23:02.551
I returned to it with the hope
of restoring this work

00:23:02.575 --> 00:23:05.777
and discovered that --
and I can only describe it this way --

00:23:05.801 --> 00:23:07.318
the life in it was gone.

00:23:07.342 --> 00:23:10.001
I opened up my book of notes.
I went through everything.

00:23:10.025 --> 00:23:12.319
There was no spark in it.
It was a pile of dust.

00:23:12.343 --> 00:23:15.128
I tried to so hard to revive that book
and it was a corpse.

00:23:15.152 --> 00:23:16.823
It just -- there was nothing to it.

00:23:16.847 --> 00:23:19.912
And then I met Ann Patchett again,

00:23:19.936 --> 00:23:22.062
only for the second time
of our acquaintance.

00:23:22.086 --> 00:23:24.958
We went out for coffee to talk
about what we were working on,

00:23:24.982 --> 00:23:28.096
and it turned out that she had
started working on a novel

00:23:28.120 --> 00:23:29.666
about the Amazon jungle.

00:23:29.690 --> 00:23:31.171
I was like, "Wow, that's crazy.